@prefix gmeow:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix owl:    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix semapv: <https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/> .
@prefix prov:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix crm:    <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/> .
@prefix as:     <https://www.w3.org/ns/activitystreams#> .
@prefix vc:     <https://www.w3.org/2018/credentials#> .

# Term equivalences for the inhabitation slice (inhabitation topology) — GMEOW
# authoring source. Compiled to mappings/gmeow-inhabitation.sssom.tsv by
# `gmeow compile-mappings`. All alignments are BY REFERENCE (Principle 5); GMEOW
# never imports an external axiom, and every external IRI is curl-validated.
#
# SCOPE DISCIPLINE (INHABITED-ALIGNMENT.md §"Aligned elsewhere, referenced
# here"): this file aligns ONLY the terms the inhabitation slice OWNS. The
# model-serving targets — OpenTelemetry-GenAI, ML-metadata, and the
# RuntimeExecution / ModelInvocation / ModelArtifact / ModelDeployment rows of
# the ledger — belong to extensions/model-serving and are authored there, not
# here (aligning a vocabulary in a slice that does not own its concept is the
# linkage twin of minting a term in the wrong place). Likewise the gUFO
# down-projection, the OWL-Time interval alignment (owned by temporal), and the
# PROV activity/agent core are GENERATED CONSTRUCT projections owned by their
# concept slices; inhabitation inherits them by reference.
#
# EVERY row here is skos:relatedMatch: the inhabitation constructs cross
# foundational categories the targets do not draw (a Situation-tenure vs a
# signed credential; a reified claim vs an E13 assignment), so none is an
# exactMatch or closeMatch — a loose lateral link, loss made explicit.

gmeow:mapsetInhabitation a gmeow:MappingSet ;
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-inhabitation.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:setId "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/mappings/inhabitation" ;
    gmeow:license "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    gmeow:setComment """Inhabitation-topology alignments (inhabitation slice).
        THE THESIS (INHABITED-ALIGNMENT.md): inhabitation is the super-structure and each external standard is a lossy shadow of it — GMEOW models the whole once and each consumer gets the view it can use. This set carries the OWN-TERM lateral links; the two flagship seams (OpenTelemetry-GenAI and W3C DID/Verifiable Credentials) are developed in full in the design set, with the OTel/runtime half owned by extensions/model-serving.
        DID / VERIFIABLE CREDENTIALS (the cryptographic-identity shadow): a gmeow:DigitalSubject is a subject of its own digital existence (Principle 9 rendered as a W3C standard) — the vc:credentialSubject a signed credential is about, identified by a DID (did:web for a vendor-hosted subject, did:key/did:pkh for a self-hosted one, recorded as provenance never privileged). A gmeow:DigitalSubjectTenure is a vc:VerifiableCredential: issuer = gmeow:tenureVantage, credentialSubject = the agent, claim = 'bears digital-subject status', proof = signature. A gmeow:IdentityContinuityAssessment 'same' across stages is a VC asserting same-subject across two DIDs, vantage-indexed — NEVER a global owl:sameAs; another issuer may decline to honour it, contestable by construction. Projection GMEOW → VC is a SoundUnderApproximation (each VC carries one signed claim; the multi-vantage continuity graph and the inhabitation topology are dropped).
        CIDOC-CRM (the cultural-heritage seam for the spiritual/fictional/legal profiles): a gmeow:InhabitationClaim is a crm:E13_Attribute_Assignment — a reified, attributed claim, a near-perfect fit that lets the heritage world document a possession or incarnation AS a documented claim, asserting no metaphysics. gmeow:ControlAssessment and gmeow:IdentityContinuityAssessment are likewise reified E13 assignments.
        ACTIVITYSTREAMS 2.0 (actor model only): a gmeow:EmbodimentCarrierRole ↔ as:Actor / its icon — the closest DEPLOYED analog to the surface a subject acts through; an inhabited host is a server hosting many actors. Scoped to the actor model: AS2's activity/content vocabulary (Create/Note/Like) is a messaging/social concern, not inhabitation's. An EmbodimentCarrierRole that is specifically an ACCOUNT reaches foaf:OnlineAccount / SIOC by reference through the accounts slice, which owns that alignment.
        PROV-O: a gmeow:TransferManifest is a prov:Entity (the transition-content record); the activity/agent/entity core of the runtime layer projects exactly and is owned by its concept slices.
        LOSS LEDGER: every row is relatedMatch (cross-category, lossy); the flagship projections are honestly SoundUnderApproximation, not 'supported' — what a target cannot hold is recorded, never silently dropped (Principles 4, 7).""" ;
    gmeow:setTrailer "# OWNED BY extensions/model-serving (landed): OpenTelemetry-GenAI (gen_ai.* spans ↔ RuntimeExecution/AgentSession/ModelDeployment/ModelArtifact) and ML-metadata (ML-Schema / Model Cards / Croissant / SPDX-AI / MLflow ↔ ModelArtifact/ModelDeployment/RuntimeExecution) are authored in slices/extensions/model-serving/mappings/equivalences.ttl, which owns those terms.\n# GENERATED CONSTRUCT projections owned elsewhere: gUFO down-projection (Principle 17), OWL-Time interval alignment (temporal slice), the PROV activity/agent core (runtime slices).\n# NO schema.org row: schema.org models no inhabitation-topology concept (subject-continuity, tenure, control, contested inhabitation claim), so aligning one would be a fabricated loose link, not a preservation-honest mapping (Principles 4, 5). The DEPLOYED surfaces that DO have a schema.org analog — an EmbodimentCarrierRole that is specifically an account — reach schema.org / foaf:OnlineAccount BY REFERENCE through the accounts slice that owns that alignment, never re-minted here." .

# --- W3C VC: the durable subject IS the subject a signed credential is about;
#     its DID is the deployed form of 'a subject of its own digital existence'.
gmeow:DigitalSubject skos:relatedMatch vc:credentialSubject {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-inhabitation.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.4 ;
    gmeow:comment "the durable digital 'who' is the vc:credentialSubject a signed credential is about, identified by a DID; a role-mixin status vs a credential subject — a loose lateral link, never exact"
|} .

# --- W3C VC: the supported-by-self-assertion tenure IS a signed, issuer-attributed
#     credential (issuer = vantage, credentialSubject = the agent, proof = signature).
gmeow:DigitalSubjectTenure skos:relatedMatch vc:VerifiableCredential {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-inhabitation.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.4 ;
    gmeow:comment "a DigitalSubjectTenure is a Verifiable Credential: issuer = tenureVantage, credentialSubject = the agent, claim = bears-digital-subject-status, proof = signature; a Situation-tenure vs a signed claim — relatedMatch only"
|} .

# --- W3C VC: the holding vantage IS the credential issuer.
gmeow:tenureVantage skos:relatedMatch vc:issuer {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-inhabitation.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.5 ;
    gmeow:comment "the frame according to which the tenure holds is the VC issuer — who asserts the status"
|} .

# --- CIDOC-CRM: a contested inhabitation is a reified, attributed E13 assignment —
#     a near-perfect fit for documenting a possession/incarnation as a claim.
gmeow:InhabitationClaim skos:relatedMatch crm:E13_Attribute_Assignment {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-inhabitation.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.5 ;
    gmeow:comment "an InhabitationClaim is a reified, attributed claim — the cultural-heritage world's E13 Attribute Assignment; lets a possession/incarnation be documented AS a claim, asserting no metaphysics"
|} .

# --- CIDOC-CRM: the descriptive continuity assessment is likewise an E13.
gmeow:IdentityContinuityAssessment skos:relatedMatch crm:E13_Attribute_Assignment {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-inhabitation.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.4 ;
    gmeow:comment "a same/different/indeterminate continuity verdict is a reified, attributed assignment (E13); also a VC asserting same-subject across two DIDs, vantage-indexed, NEVER a global owl:sameAs"
|} .

# --- CIDOC-CRM: the control assessment is a reified, attributed E13 as well.
gmeow:ControlAssessment skos:relatedMatch crm:E13_Attribute_Assignment {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-inhabitation.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.4 ;
    gmeow:comment "who-was-driving is a reified, attributed assignment (E13); attributed agency, not deception — a documented similarity, no axiom coupling"
|} .

# --- ActivityStreams 2.0 (actor model only): the surface a subject acts through.
gmeow:EmbodimentCarrierRole skos:relatedMatch as:Actor {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-inhabitation.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.4 ;
    gmeow:comment "the carrier surface (device/avatar/account/terminal/voice/channel) ↔ as:Actor / its icon — the closest deployed analog; the actor model only, not AS2's activity/content vocabulary; an account-typed carrier reaches foaf:OnlineAccount/SIOC via the accounts slice"
|} .

# --- PROV-O: the transition-content record is a prov:Entity.
gmeow:TransferManifest skos:relatedMatch prov:Entity {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-inhabitation.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.5 ;
    gmeow:comment "the coarse-grained record of what crossed a migration boundary is a prov:Entity, referenced by the transition Activity; the per-item wasDerivedFrom edges are already PROV-aligned"
|} .
